  "scope": "Both public claim entry coordinators, local-image correspondence diagnostics and optional-lease backpressure mapping move to the product adapter. Native owners retain atomic issuance, fairness, live capacity and counters, plus single-entry cache adoption after commit.",
  "limitations": [
    "Trusted product policy, not raw ingress or the standalone generic VM. Caller permissions, bounded input, clock provenance and consistent worker limits remain native obligations. Cache correspondence does not grant a lease.",
    "A local cache conflict may be returned after the journal has committed a lease. The coordinator never retries hooks, refunds delivery attempts or rolls back prior native effects; journal transactions retain their own rollback boundaries.",
    "The frozen entries share the existing clock kernels, diagnostic mappings and journal machinery. This proves coordinator compatibility, not independent implementation of the scheduler or storage layers.",
    "Native result conversion/settlement, journal ownership, complete host-neutral durable recovery, vertical compatibility and physical extraction remain open. Native completion and maturity are unchanged.",
    "Local macOS Rust/SQLite verification only; no Linux, GUI or remote CI run. The existing 280-file standalone checkpoint was integrity-checked, not freshly exported or retested."
  ],
